<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00889</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>37d9d69b-b331-4d77-810f-4b34f6976c08</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="c4f6daa0-50bc-428c-8cf5-7a097e999cc1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>1. Function \(f\) gives the temperature, in degrees Celsius, \(t\) hours after midnight.</para>
            <para>Choose which equation or expression represents the statement in function notation.</para>
            <para>The temperature was the same at 9 a.m. and at 4 p.m.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(9)=f(4)\)</para>
            <para>\(f(9)=f(16)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(9)=f(16)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(9)=f(16)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b4bd3db2-dbdc-421d-b42e-bb285b895f47" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>It was warmer at 9 a.m. than at 6 a.m.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(9)\) &gt; \(f(6)\)</para>
            <para>\(f(9)\)&lt;\(f(6)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(9) &gt; f(6)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(9) &gt; f(6)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_98400bad-9f27-4e0d-8430-f67c0ae26c26" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Some time after midnight, the temperature was 24 degrees Celsius.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(24)=t\)</para>
            <para>\(f(0)&lt;24\)</para>
            <para>\(f(t)=24\)</para>
            <para>\(f(12)=24\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(t)=24\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(t)=24\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_2b429285-9e48-4744-8816-9fc39d073d9a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Select the <emphasis>two</emphasis> points that are on the graph of \(f\) if we know that \(f(2)=-4\) and \(f(5)=3.4\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \((2, -4)\), \((5, 3.4)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8a768d37-c781-46a7-b425-c2bc929041e4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>

            <para>Looking at the graph of the function \(g\), below, which is greater, \(g(-5)\) or \(g(5)\)?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(g(-5)\)</para>
            <para>\(g(5)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(g(-5)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.1.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(g(-5)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1237bb5b-2130-4f17-8364-9a5468a6d902" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The function \(T\) tells how many people are living on floor \(n\) of an apartment building. What does \(T(4)=82\) mean?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! There are 82 people living on floor 4.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.2.1-4.2.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: There are 82 people living on floor 4.
    </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_2dc2c733-5dfb-4762-81ad-c238a622c7b0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The function, \(T\), gives the temperature of a house, in degrees Fahrenheit, \(h\) hours after midnight. Choose which function notation represents the temperature at 6 a.m. was 70 degrees.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(T(70)=6\)</para>
            <para>\(T(6)=70\)</para>
            <para>\(6(T)=70\)</para>
            <para>\(70(T)=6\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(T(6)=70\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(T(6)=70\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b1d1f02d-f133-416a-a9a6-4be309380f15" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The graph below represents a function, \(f\), which gives the height of a drone, in meters, \(t\) seconds after it leaves the ground. Which statement describes the point \(f(2)=4\)?</para>
                  <media alt="Graph. Horizontal axis, 0 to 8, time, seconds. Vertical axis, height, meters. Starting at 0 comma 0, the graph increases linearly. From 2 to 6, it’s horizontal. Then decreases linearly to 7 comma 0.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_06_10_01.svg"/>
              </media>
            
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The height of the drone after 2 seconds is 4 meters off the ground.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.3.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: The height of the drone after 2 seconds is 4 meters off the ground.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
